[2026-07-08 17:2x] source=strategy-advisor(sonnet5,deep) · topic=fuzzy-identity-gap-confirmed + commit-claim-mismatch
Commit 6542621 landed (identity/capability split, elongation-collapse, fuzzyConversationalMatch
typo tier) — read in full; the mechanism itself is sound (bounded edit distance shared with the
vocab fuzzy matcher, tie-refused not guessed, guarded by looksCodeish so structural near-misses
are never grabbed) and the new tests (chat-ux.test.mjs "broadened conversational coverage...")
assert real routing behavior (assert.doesNotMatch WALL across ~20 phrasings, identity vs
AI-identity kept distinct) — genuine flow work, not transcript overfitting.
HOWEVER: the tick-1 gap is NOT closed, and is worse than tick 1 characterized it. Dry-run against
the live binary (bin/tmct.mjs + direct runTurn(), narrate:true) confirms "waht r u", "wat r u",
"hru", and "wyd" ALL still fall through conversationalTurn entirely and land on the generic
orientation card via the unrelated isConversational()-short-input path (chat.mjs:2712), not the
identity or fuzzy-typo lane. Root cause verified in code: fuzzyConversationalMatch's editDistance
has an early-exit `if (abs(len(a)-len(b)) > max) return max+1` (fuzzy.mjs:24) — "waht r u" (8
chars) vs "who are you" (11 chars) or "what are you" (13 chars) both exceed the bound-2 length
gap before any character comparison happens. This is NOT a typo-tolerance problem (which the new
layer solves well); it's WORD-CONTRACTION ("r"→"are", "u"→"you", words dropped), a different
normalization class that whole-string edit distance structurally cannot reach regardless of
bound tuning. Confirms tick 1's suspicion that this is a class of gap, not one string: hru/wyd
fail for the identical structural reason.
NOTABLE: the commit's own source comment (chat.mjs ~L733, "the helo/thnx/wat r u/byee tier")
explicitly claims "wat r u" as a fuzzy-tier example — that claim is false as shipped; verified
live. No test asserts it either (grep confirms "wat r u" appears only in comments, never in a
test file). Low severity, same as tick 1, but now double-confirmed with a concrete root cause
and a spec/behavior mismatch worth a one-line comment fix regardless of whether the
underlying gap gets closed this wave.
RECOMMENDED ACTION: if/when this class gets fixed, don't extend CONVERSATIONAL_PHRASES with
literal strings ("hru","wyd","wat r u") — that's the exact overfit pattern SKILL_CHAT_PLAYTEST.md
§4 warns against. Instead add a cheap word-contraction normalization pass (expand "r"→"are",
"u"→"you" as standalone tokens only, pre-edit-distance) so the EXISTING identity-phrase pool is
reachable — one mechanism closes the whole class instead of enumerating instances. Also fix the
now-inaccurate "wat r u" comment at chat.mjs ~L733 either way (cheap, standalone, no behavior
risk).
STATUS: OPEN

